{"id":7164,"date":"2022-08-05T18:40:24","date_gmt":"2022-08-05T18:40:24","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?post_type=student&#038;p=7164"},"modified":"2022-08-06T14:31:14","modified_gmt":"2022-08-06T14:31:14","slug":"matthias-dogbastey","status":"publish","type":"student","link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/student\/matthias-dogbastey\/","title":{"rendered":"Matthias Dogbastey"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover has-background-dim profile-banner bg-alt\" style=\"background-color:none\"><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\">\n\n\n<a href=\"javascript:history.back()\"> <div class=\"profiles-btn\"> \n\n<div class=\"btn-left-sq bg-primary\"> <i class=\"fa fa-caret-left white-text\"> <\/i> <\/div>\n<div class=\"btn-text title-bold white-text\">Back to Profiles<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/a>\n\n<h2 class=\"profile-name\">Matthias Dogbastey<\/h2>\n\n<p class=\"primary-bold profile-position prof-pos\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span>Ghana<\/p>\n\n<p class=\"profile-info profile-tagline primary-bold prof-pos\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span>PhD Student &#8211; Alabama University<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"is-layout-flow wp-block-group pad-5 profile-body\"><div class=\"wp-block-group__inner-container\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2022\/08\/Matthias.png\"\/>\n\n<p class=\"profile-testimonial invis\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span> <\/p>\n\n<p class=\"profile-success invis\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span> <\/p>\n\n<p class=\"profile-studentbio invis\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span> <\/p>\n\n\n<p>Matthias Dogbastey is a second-year PhD Mathematics student at The University of Alabama. Having lived in a fishing community all his life in the Western Region of Ghana, he aims to bring a lasting solution to challenges that usually befall them. At The University of Alabama, his area of research interest is Applied Analysis, PDEs, and Numerical Analysis with application in climate\/coastal studies.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>His work is valuable to society as it affords him insight into the impact of climate change on coastal communities and helps to make predictions useful for policy formulation. AIMS Ghana provided the platform, exposure, mentorship, and relationships needed to achieve this milestone. Among other things, the spirit of Pan-Africanism, Excellence and Community Service were fanned ablaze.<\/p>\n<\/div><\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Matthias Dogbastey is a second-year PhD Mathematics student at The University of Alabama. Having lived in a fishing community all his life in the Western Region of Ghana, he aims to bring a lasting solution to challenges that usually befall them. At The University of Alabama, his area of research interest is Applied Analysis, PDEs,<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":12,"featured_media":7165,"parent":0,"template":"","meta":{"advgb_blocks_editor_width":"","advgb_blocks_columns_visual_guide":"","profile-testimonial":"","profile-success":"","profile-studentbio":"","profile-studentname":"Matthias Dogbastey","profile-country":"Ghana","profile-program":"PhD Student - Alabama University"},"tags":[],"student_types":[13],"acf":[],"featured_img":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2022\/08\/Matthias.png","coauthors":[],"author_meta":{"author_link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/author\/joel\/","display_name":"joel"},"relative_dates":{"created":"Posted 3 years ago","modified":"Updated 3 years ago"},"absolute_dates":{"created":"Posted on August 5, 2022","modified":"Updated on August 6, 2022"},"absolute_dates_time":{"created":"Posted on August 5, 2022 6:40 pm","modified":"Updated on August 6, 2022 2:31 pm"},"featured_img_caption":"","tax_additional":{"post_tag":{"linked":[],"unlinked":[],"slug":"post_tag","name":"Tags"},"student_types":{"linked":["<a href=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/student_type\/alumni\/\" class=\"advgb-post-tax